---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import SimpleBackground from '../components/SimpleBackground.astro'
---

<Layout>
  <SimpleBackground />

  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-12 relative z-10">
    <div
      class="fixed top-6 left-0 right-0 z-50 px-6 flex justify-center pointer-events-none"
    >
      <nav
        class="pointer-events-auto flex justify-between items-center bg-background/60 backdrop-blur-2xl border border-border/50 rounded-full px-6 py-3 shadow-2xl shadow-black/5 w-full max-w-7xl"
      >
        <a
          href="/sanctuary/"
          class="text-xl font-black tracking-tighter flex items-center gap-2 text-foreground hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity"
        >
          <i data-lucide="moon-star" class="text-primary w-5 h-5"></i>
          Sanctuary
        </a>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-6 md:gap-8">
          <a
            href="/sanctuary/guides"
            class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary transition-colors"
            >Guides</a
          >
          <a
            href="https://github.com/rajeshepili/sanctuary/releases"
            class="px-5 py-2.5 rounded-full font-bold text-[10px] sm:text-xs uppercase tracking-widest bg-primary text-primary-foreground shadow-lg shadow-primary/20 hover:scale-105 active:scale-95 transition-all"
            >Download</a
          >
        </div>
      </nav>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-16 pb-32 pt-32">
      <aside class="lg:col-span-3">
        <div class="sticky top-32 space-y-12">
          <div>
            <h2
              class="text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground mb-4"
            >
              Using Sanctuary
            </h2>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              <li>
                <a href="#getting-started" class="text-sm font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Getting started</a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="#privacy" class="text-sm font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Privacy & PIN</a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="#habits" class="text-sm font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Habits</a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="#backups" class="text-sm font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Backups & exports</a>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2
              class="text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground mb-4"
            >
              Developers
            </h2>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              <li>
                <a href="#architecture" class="text-sm font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">How it's built</a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="#building" class="text-sm font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Build from source</a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="https://github.com/rajeshepili/sanctuary/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md" class="text-sm font-medium hover:text-primary transition-colors">Architecture doc ↗</a>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <main class="lg:col-span-9 space-y-32">
        <header>
          <h1 class="text-6xl lg:text-8xl font-black tracking-tighter leading-[0.9] mb-8">
            Guides
          </h1>
          <p class="text-2xl text-muted-foreground max-w-2xl font-serif italic">
            How to install Sanctuary, keep your data safe, and hack on the code if you want to.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="space-y-24">
          <section id="getting-started" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-4 border-b border-foreground/10 pb-4 mb-8">
              <i data-lucide="compass" class="text-primary w-6 h-6"></i>
              <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Getting started</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
              Grab an installer from
              <a href="https://github.com/rajeshepili/sanctuary/releases" class="text-primary hover:underline">GitHub Releases</a>
              — AppImage or deb on Linux, dmg on macOS, exe on Windows. No account needed. The app works offline after install.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
              First launch walks you through a few setup steps: what to show on your dashboard, the privacy disclaimer, an optional PIN, and where to store backups.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="privacy" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-4 border-b border-foreground/10 pb-4 mb-8">
              <i data-lucide="lock" class="text-primary w-6 h-6"></i>
              <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Privacy & PIN</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
              Your entries live in a SQLite file on your computer. Nothing is uploaded unless you explicitly export or set up folder sync.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
              <strong>Settings → App Lock</strong> adds a 4-digit PIN when opening the app. It is stored as a salted SHA-256 hash locally. Handy if you share a computer; not a substitute for disk encryption.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="habits" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-4 border-b border-foreground/10 pb-4 mb-8">
              <i data-lucide="calendar" class="text-primary w-6 h-6"></i>
              <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Habits</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
              Sanctuary measures consistency over a rolling window (30 days by default), not a single streak counter. Missing a day lowers your percentage a bit instead of wiping progress to zero.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
              Use rest mode when you need time off. The habit picks up again when you are ready.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="backups" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-4 border-b border-foreground/10 pb-4 mb-8">
              <i data-lucide="archive" class="text-primary w-6 h-6"></i>
              <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Backups & exports</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
              Turn on scheduled backups in <strong>Settings → Backup & Data</strong>. By default files go to <code class="text-sm bg-foreground/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">~/Documents/Sanctuary Backups</code> as dated JSON files.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
              You can also export Markdown or a full JSON snapshot from the same screen. If you leave Sanctuary, take an export with you — there is no cloud account to log back into.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-24 pt-32">
          <section id="architecture" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-4 border-b border-foreground/10 pb-4 mb-8">
              <i data-lucide="cpu" class="text-primary w-6 h-6"></i>
              <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">How it's built</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
              Electron opens the window and starts a small Nitro server on localhost. The React UI talks to that server over HTTP. SQLite holds your data; Drizzle runs migrations on startup.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
              Each request from the app window carries a session token generated at launch so random browser tabs cannot hit your local API.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="building" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-4 border-b border-foreground/10 pb-4 mb-8">
              <i data-lucide="code" class="text-primary w-6 h-6"></i>
              <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Build from source</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
              Node 22+, pnpm, then:
            </p>
            <pre class="bg-foreground/5 p-6 rounded-xl overflow-x-auto font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed"><code>git clone https://github.com/rajeshepili/sanctuary
cd sanctuary
pnpm install
pnpm dev:desktop</code></pre>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
              See <a href="https://github.com/rajeshepili/sanctuary/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md" class="text-primary hover:underline">CONTRIBUTING.md</a> for tests, lint, and release builds.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </main>
    </div>

    <footer class="py-12 border-t border-foreground/10 flex justify-between items-center text-[10px] font-black tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-muted-foreground">
      <div>Sanctuary / Guides</div>
      <a href="/sanctuary/" class="hover:text-primary transition-colors">Back to home</a>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Layout>
